✗ layer violation

    internal/notes/domain/note.go:3
      package example.com/fix/internal/notes/domain          (layer: domain)
        imports example.com/fix/internal/notes/infrastructure (layer: infrastructure)

  The domain layer imports nothing from the other three — that rule is
  why the domain can be tested, versioned, and extracted on its own.

  Fix one of:
    • Move the type you need into the domain, and let the other layer
      depend on it.
    • Declare a port in the domain and implement it in infrastructure,
      then wire the two in module.go — the one file permitted to see
      all four layers.

1 violation(s) in 2 packages.

  NOT checked: the cross-module rule. It compares feature modules, which it
  finds by a `modules` path segment — internal/modules/<feature>/… , the tree
  `warren new` generates — and this project has none, so nothing was compared
  across features.
